  "interpretation": "Counters exactly fit one 4 KiB singleton coalesced object per fsync and 32 additional ordinary 4 MiB objects. Reviewed flat-v1 mount with allowlisted environment uses the frozen code defaults: target 65536 bytes, first-member wait 100 ms. A single synchronous fio job cannot contribute another write before its fsync completes; 1 MiB sequential slices exceed the target. The timing and byte fingerprint support the queue deadline as the leading explanation.",
  "limitations": [
    "Counters are aggregated within a bounded subwindow of one run, not per-operation joins, Redis timings, or S3 object-key traces. No object roles or clocks are matched.",
    "Sequential reference is a cumulative scrape within its own run, not a cross-run aligned window. Raw fio latency statistics are independent full-job totals.",
    "The 32 additional PUTs are consistent with ordinary 4 MiB frames; their cause is not established. The conditional 100 ms notification timeout is a separate path; no per-request trace isolates it.",
    "A future fixed-durability test changing only the queue deadline or disabling new coalesced groups, or key/magic and per-request timing evidence, can falsify this attribution. No new run was made."
  ]
